WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.680
You need three celery stalks with leaves, three clear glasses, and blue or red food

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.680
colouring.

3
00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:11.843
Fill each glass with about five centimetres of water.

4
00:00:12.323 --> 00:00:15.543
Stir in 15 to 20 drops of colouring per glass.

5
00:00:16.103 --> 00:00:18.203
An adult trims the bottom of each stalk.

6
00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:21.303
Stand them in a bright spot, out of direct sun.

7
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.947
Check after about four hours.

8
00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.987
Most often, coloured lines show along the stalk.

9
00:00:27.607 --> 00:00:32.287
Overnight usually gives the clearest result, and the cut end shows a row of coloured

10
00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:33.287
dots.

11
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.770
Stay nearby while the coloured water is out.

12
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.470
An adult does all the cutting.
